Q = [
make(1, "Mia will ___ her presentation tonight, so she checks the slides and practices twice. What does the blank mean?", {"A": "get it ready", "B": "throw it away", "C": "hide it from everyone", "D": "forget the topic"}, "A", "Checking slides and practicing show that Mia is getting the presentation ready; prepare means get something ready.", "Use the actions before and after the blank to infer the verb instead of translating it alone.", ["Read the whole sentence and identify Mia's actions.", "Notice that checking and practicing happen before the presentation.", "Match those actions with get something ready.", "Reject throw away, hide, and forget because they conflict with the actions.", "Choose A and reread the sentence to confirm the meaning."], "easy"),
make(2, "Leo asks, 'May I ___ your ruler for one minute?' His classmate says yes and expects it back. What does borrow mean?", {"A": "use something temporarily and return it", "B": "buy something permanently", "C": "break something on purpose", "D": "draw a ruler from memory"}, "A", "Leo wants to use the ruler briefly and return it, which is the classroom meaning of borrow.", "Look for the time limit and the expected action after use; those clues separate borrow from buy or keep.", ["Identify the object Leo wants.", "Use for one minute as a temporary-use clue.", "Use expects it back as the return clue.", "Compare the clues with all four choices.", "Choose A because temporary use followed by return defines borrow."], "easy"),
make(3, "The teacher says, 'Please ___ the library book by Friday.' Which word best completes the instruction?", {"A": "return", "B": "invite", "C": "protect", "D": "repair"}, "A", "A student returns a library book by giving it back; the deadline by Friday supports that meaning.", "Identify what normally happens to the object and use the deadline as a contextual clue.", ["Identify the object as a library book.", "Ask what a student does with a borrowed book by a deadline.", "Match give it back with return.", "Eliminate invite, protect, and repair because none means give back.", "Choose A and read the complete instruction again."], "easy"),
make(4, "Our group will ___ the new student to join the science game. Which word means ask someone to take part?", {"A": "invite", "B": "arrive", "C": "decide", "D": "borrow"}, "A", "To invite someone is to ask that person to come or participate; joining the game is the direct clue.", "Use the purpose phrase to identify the verb's social function.", ["Locate the person affected: the new student.", "Locate the requested action: join the game.", "Ask which verb means ask someone to participate.", "Eliminate arrive, decide, and borrow as unrelated actions.", "Select A and check that invite the student is grammatical."], "easy"),
make(5, "The hallway is so ___ that two classes cannot pass at the same time. Which adjective fits best?", {"A": "crowded", "B": "silent", "C": "empty", "D": "private"}, "A", "If two classes cannot pass because there are too many people or things, the hallway is crowded.", "Use the consequence in the second clause to infer the physical condition.", ["Read the result: two classes cannot pass together.", "Infer that the space has too many people or objects.", "Match that condition with crowded.", "Remove silent, empty, and private because they do not mean full of people.", "Choose A and reread the hallway sentence."], "easy"),
make(6, "During the listening test, the teacher asks everyone to remain ___. Which choice means making very little or no sound?", {"A": "quiet", "B": "early", "C": "careful", "D": "ready"}, "A", "During a listening test, making little or no sound is described as quiet.", "Connect the classroom instruction with the behavior required at that moment.", ["Identify the situation as a listening test.", "Ask what behavior helps everyone hear the recording.", "Match making little or no sound with quiet.", "Reject early, careful, and ready because they do not name sound level.", "Choose A and read remain quiet as a complete instruction."], "easy"),
make(7, "The art teacher will ___ the broken model before the exhibition. What does repair mean?", {"A": "fix it", "B": "label it", "C": "borrow it", "D": "move it to another school"}, "A", "A broken model that will be displayed needs to be fixed; repair means fix.", "Use broken and the future exhibition to infer the needed action.", ["Find the model's condition: it is broken.", "Find the purpose: it will be displayed later.", "Ask what action makes a broken model usable.", "Compare fix with label, borrow, and move.", "Select A and verify repair the model is natural English."], "medium"),
make(8, "The bus leaves at 7:30, so students must ___ at the school gate by 7:20. Which word fits?", {"A": "arrive", "B": "return", "C": "protect", "D": "prepare"}, "A", "Students need to reach the gate before a stated time; arrive means reach a place.", "Use the place and time information to distinguish arriving from preparing or returning.", ["Identify the destination as the school gate.", "Identify the deadline as 7:20.", "Ask which verb means reach a place before that time.", "Eliminate return, protect, and prepare.", "Choose A and check arrive at the gate as the correct phrase."], "easy"),
make(9, "The class discusses two poster designs and finally chooses the blue one. What did the class do?", {"A": "decide", "B": "repair", "C": "invite", "D": "borrow"}, "A", "After discussing alternatives and choosing one, the class made a decision; decide is the required verb.", "Follow the sequence of considering options and selecting one.", ["Notice that there are two possible designs.", "Notice that discussion comes before selection.", "Interpret choosing one as making a decision.", "Remove repair, invite, and borrow because they do not describe selection.", "Select A and reread decide on the blue one in context."], "medium"),
make(10, "The students put a cover on the microscope and carry it with both hands. They want to ___ it. Which word means keep it safe from harm?", {"A": "protect", "B": "arrive", "C": "crowd", "D": "return"}, "A", "Covering and carrying the microscope carefully are actions that protect it from harm.", "Use the physical actions as evidence of the intended purpose.", ["Identify the object that needs care: the microscope.", "List the actions: cover it and carry it with both hands.", "Infer the purpose of those actions: prevent damage.", "Match prevent damage with protect and reject the other verbs.", "Choose A and confirm protect the microscope is natural."], "medium"),
]

